.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt PAMAUTH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pamauth
.Nd PAM password checks for the ChatServer XMPP service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lets users sign in to ChatServer, the jabberd2 XMPP server, with their
system account.
The c2s component starts it when
.Pa c2s.xml
selects the
.Dq pipe
authreg module with
.Nm
as its program, and sends it one request per line on standard input:
.Bl -tag -width "CHECK-PASSWORD user password realm"
.It Li USER-EXISTS Ar user realm
Answers
.Li OK
if
.Xr getpwnam 3
finds
.Ar user ,
otherwise
.Li NO .
.It Li CHECK-PASSWORD Ar user password realm
Checks the base64-encoded
.Ar password
with the
.Xr pam 3
service
.Dq jabberd ,
running both its auth and account parts.
Answers
.Li OK
or
.Li NO .
.It Li FREE
Exits.
.El
.Pp
The realm is ignored.
Results are logged to
.Xr syslog 3
with the auth facility.
.Pp
.Xr pam_unix 8
can only check passwords as root, so
.Nm
is installed setuid root and can be run only by the
.Dq jabber
group, which lets c2s itself run without privileges.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/pam.d/jabberd -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pam.d/jabberd
The PAM policy.
To let only the members of one group sign in, add
.Xr pam_group 8
to its account part.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jabber_autobuddy 8 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr pam_group 8 ,
.Xr pam_unix 8
.Sh HISTORY
Apple's ChatServer, the jabberd2 build in OS X Server, checked passwords
against Open Directory.
.Nm
replaces that for the FreeBSD port.
